    fix(EUDPA-304): update outbox e2e tests for NotificationEdited page-save events (#105)
    
    * fix(EUDPA-304): update outbox e2e tests for NotificationEdited page-save events
    
    Page saves now emit NotificationEdited, so tests that asserted on total
    outbox event counts or assumed aggregateVersion=1 for lifecycle events
    no longer hold.
    
    - Delete "does not write an outbox event before submission" — the
      invariant it tested no longer exists and a negative poll is flaky
    - outbox-event-notification: filter by eventType=NotificationSubmitted
      when polling and fetching; remove toHaveLength(1) and aggregateVersion=1
    - admin-outbox-events: filter table row by NotificationSubmitted text
      rather than assuming it is always row 0
    - outbox-event-amendment: query by eventType=NotificationSubmissionAmended
      directly; change aggregateVersion assertion from toBe(2) to toBeGreaterThan(1)
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * EUDPA-304 - Update tests to account for draft status in status change list
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: ian.griffiths <ian.griffiths@defra.onmicrosoft.com>
